# Turret (a light tower): strikes the nearest SOLID enemy unit in range with a column of light; each shot spends
# "Turret shot energy" from its internal store - defense output rides the supply network.
# Spawned origin 2.0 above ground.
# SHAPE (a placeholder; uniform scales of the baseshapes variants): a stone OBELISK - a wide foot (the root), a thick
# lower shaft and a thin upper one, each with a bronze collar, and a cold blue crystal at the tip, 5.6 m over the
# ground. The child pieces are render-only; the collider is the 4x4x4 m box. Keep the `Head` height in step with
# beamHeightOf(Turret) in Game/Private/Light.cpp and c_turretMuzzle in GameStructureComponent.cpp.
Prefab gameTurret
	Global true
	Component Render
		ObjectContainer baseshapes
		Node CubeHalf
		Type StaticMesh
		Color 0.5 0.48 0.44
		Position 0 -1.3 0
		Scale 1.4
	Component Physics
		Body Static
		ContactEvents true
		Shape Box
		HalfExtents 2 2 2
	Component GameStructure
		AlwaysShowResources true
		MeleeRadius 2
